FINAL IMPLEMENTATION NOTE
•	All departments should be configurable according to company type and business size.
•	Small businesses can activate only Accounts, Inventory, Sales, Procurement and HR.
•	Trading businesses can additionally activate Distribution, WMS, Logistics and CRM.
•	Manufacturing businesses can activate Production, BOM, MRP, QC, Costing and Maintenance.
•	Schools and colleges can activate Admissions, Academics, Examination, Student Fees, Faculty and Student Records.
•	Hospitals can activate Patient Registration, OPD, IPD, Laboratory, Pharmacy, Billing and Insurance.
•	Construction and solar companies can activate Projects, Site Operations, BOQ, Material Management, Installation and Costing.
•	Each department should have its own Dashboard, Definition, Master Data, Forms, Reports, Approval Workflow and Access Permissions.
•	Every form should open in a separate popup / window or dedicated form screen.
•	Every report should open in a separate report viewer with filters, preview, drill-down, print and export functionality.
•	All transactions should update relevant departments automatically through controlled workflows.
•	Accounting entries, inventory movements, audit logs and approval history should be linked with their original source transactions.
•	Departments, forms, fields, reports and permissions should be configurable; not every industry needs every module.

